Subject: [PATCH] fonts: preserve static design precision in Fontations

Linux's normal FCI font manager uses the Fontations scanner, so the existing
FreeType-only precision branch does not cover its browser glyphs. Use the
existing cache-keyed Mac-profile design-space flag in the actual Fontations
scaler. Preserve the backend, font data and default/native/Windows path.

For eligible static, unhinted outline faces, request the existing outline
extractor at UPEM and scale design coordinates in double before float storage.
Scale static hmtx advances directly from checked design-unit fields instead of
skrifa's FreeType-compatible fixed scaling. Preserve the remaining matrix and
path-modified semantics. Variables, synthesized bold, autohinting requests,
hinting-reliant fonts, and color/SVG/bitmap/hybrid faces retain their baseline.
No profile lookup or new bridge API is introduced inside Skia.

Add separate factory-direct Fontations GTests and resources. Existing0053
FreeType tests are unchanged. Update the SkFont flag documentation to cover
its Fontations static advances. No dependency on the archived0054 candidate.

